      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "We are reviewing this internally.\n\nAs an aside, I will mention that there is essentially zero benefit for a texture size above 2k in most cases, especially when viewed in VR. Unless your face is directly against the texture, it can be difficult to tell the difference.\n\nUntil this is looked at and evaluated I would suggest that you refrain from using textures on your model that are that large... there's not much point to it. :) Creating atlases with UVs sizes based on surface area should provide more than enough detail where you need it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
